.TH "FWD PUSH" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd push Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-push \- Mirror local changes up to the remote session; remote-only
files are deleted unless sync.delete is off.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd push
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mirror local changes up to the remote session; remote-only files are
deleted unless sync.delete is off.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name <str>
Session name, target, or backend; defaults to this directory's session.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
